0..34 Comment "/// A transport along a held call."
35..38 Comment "///"
39..116 Comment "/// A composite whose second path is a stuck call is one composite, and so is"
117..192 Comment "/// an action on that call. The call may stand alone or behind an identity,"
193..219 Comment "/// and the kernel agrees."
220..223 Comment "///"
224..293 Comment "/// The append runs a held operand and writes a bind over its call. A"
294..368 Comment "/// transport along the held path is a bind over the same call. So the two"
369..440 Comment "/// compare by the call, then by the transports under one variable. Two"
441..515 Comment "/// actions write the call in their motives, which compare by its function"
516..533 Comment "/// and argument."
534..537 Comment "///"
538..636 Comment "/// - see: #3800 — the checker declined two composites that differ only by a call of an identity"
637..729 Comment "/// - see: #3802 — the code walk compares two written calls by their function and argument"
730..816 Comment "/// - see: #3807 — the checker refused two actions whose motives each write the call"
818..860 Comment "/// The identity on paths from `x` to `y`."
